  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q77-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Complete the square of $x^4+4$, and hence factorise it to a product of two quadratic expressions.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Completed square: $(x^2+2)^2-4x^2$.\nFactorisation: $(x^2-2x+2)(x^2+2x+2)$.\n\nAdd and subtract $4x^2$, then use the difference of squares.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^4+4&=x^4+4x^2+4-4x^2\\\\x^4+4&=(x^2+2)^2-(2x)^2\\\\x^4+4&=(x^2+2-2x)(x^2+2+2x)\\\\x^4+4&=(x^2-2x+2)(x^2+2x+2).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
